venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw and intermediate rasters are large and fully reproducible from
# run_pipeline.py -- the full multi-year archive (344MB: every year back
# to 2005, used only to build the historical trend numbers already baked
# into stats.json) stays out of git. But the *current-year* files the
# live map actually reads at render time -- one year's true-colour/NDVI/
# land-cover/SAR/elevation rasters plus the BRP parcel geometry -- are a
# real ~58MB, not 344MB, and are carved out below so a fresh deploy (e.g.
# Streamlit Community Cloud) gets a working map immediately, not just the
# stats.json-only numbers/charts. `data/raw/*` and `data/processed/*` (not
# a trailing-slash directory pattern) are deliberate -- a directory
# pattern stops git from ever looking inside it, which would make every
# `!` negation below silently do nothing.
#
# Known limitation, not fixed here: these filenames are pinned to the
# *current* pipeline year (summer_2025/2024/2026, sar_2025, the
# 2018-2026 change map, the 2024-01-16 flood peak). Next time
# run_pipeline.py's "current year" rolls forward, this list needs the
# same rollover -- update the filenames below to match, or the newly
# generated current-year files won't be tracked and the deploy will fall
# back to the graceful "run the pipeline locally" message again.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/villages.geojson
!data/raw/summer_2025.tif
!data/raw/brp_parcels.geojson
!data/raw/no2.tif
!data/raw/dtm_05m.tif
!data/raw/ndsm_05m.tif
data/processed/*
!data/processed/stats.json
!data/processed/summer_2025_indices.tif
!data/processed/summer_2025_landcover.tif
!data/processed/summer_2025_landcover_legend.txt
!data/processed/ndvi_change_summer_2024_to_summer_2025.tif
!data/processed/sar_2025_indices.tif
!data/processed/flood_extent_sar_highwater_2024.tif
!data/processed/flood_changedetect_sar_event_20240116.tif
!data/processed/landcover_change_2018_2026.tif
outputs/*.png
outputs/*.html
*.docx
